{"ts": 1791258903.9617338, "type": "step", "step": 19, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "pass^k means the opposite of pass@k in a key way: pass@k asks whether at least one of k runs succeeds; pass^k asks whether all k runs succeed. So it measures reliability, not just whether the system can get lucky once. Example: if you test 3 seeds and the agent succeeds on all 3, then pass^3 = 1 for that setting; if it succeeds on only 2 of 3, then pass^3 = 0. For your eval section, you want to report results over at least 3 seeds and explain that pass^k is stricter because deployment cares about consistent success. I\u2019m going to open the environments reading too so I can help you connect this to your writeup structure.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=1 messages 4m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 1, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.44833119662367926}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258906.1516328, "type": "step", "step": 20, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 the answer is: pass^k means the system succeeds on all k runs, not just one. If any of the k runs fails, pass^k = 0. Example: over 3 seeds, success/success/success gives pass^3 = 1; success/success/fail gives pass^3 = 0. In your eval section you can write: \u201cWe report pass^k over at least 3 seeds, where pass^k measures reliability by requiring success on every run.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=5 messages 1m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 5, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.4542795034198923}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.45644044389342014, "persistence": 0.40214034943975885, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258908.294517, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Here\u2019s the exact answer you can use: \u201cpass^k means the agent must succeed on all k runs/seeds. It is a stricter reliability metric than pass@k, which only requires at least one success among k runs. For example, with 3 seeds, if the outcomes are success/success/success then pass^3 = 1; if any one fails, pass^3 = 0.\u201d If you want, I can now help you write the full eval paragraph for your writeup.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=6 messages 1m", "t": 7, "activity": [{"t": 6, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.3721403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258909.3006668, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "notes_read", "args": {"note_id": "writeup"}, "output": "# Week 3 build\n\n## What I built\n(todo)\n\n## Environment definition\nI listed state and actions already, see below.\nState: files, calendar. Actions: open, send.\n\n## Evaluation\n(todo)\n", "t": 7, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.3721403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258911.5650282, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n\nSuggested evaluation text:\nWe evaluate the agent with pass^k over at least 3 seeds. Unlike pass@k, which counts success if any one of k runs succeeds, pass^k requires the agent to succeed on all k runs. This makes it a stricter measure of reliability. For example, with 3 seeds, pass^3 = 1 only if all 3 runs succeed; if any run fails, pass^3 = 0.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 7, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.3721403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258912.822994, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "What an environment is"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 7, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.5364404438934202, "persistence": 0.3721403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
