{"ts": 1791258928.945462, "type": "step", "step": 33, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 the answer is: a POMDP means the agent does not observe the full underlying state, only partial observations. In your build, the full state includes things like all files, unread messages, calendar, and even student attention, but the assistant only sees what is on screen or what it opens. So it must act under uncertainty and gather information. One sentence you can use: \u201cThis environment is a POMDP because the assistant only gets partial observations of the full state and must take actions to reveal more.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-environment"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=30 feed 1m", "t": 31, "activity": [{"t": 30, "app": "feed", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.5407251856436682, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.75, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7724817897604411, "motivation": 0.444715486329607, "reliance": 0.6164404438934201, "persistence": 0.3421403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 1, "feed_minutes": 1.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.1411732999999997, "seen_posts": ["p6"], "extra": {}}}
