{"ts": 1791258935.029703, "type": "step", "step": 36, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Here\u2019s the simplest version:\n\n- pass^k: the agent must succeed every time across k runs.\n- POMDP: the agent cannot see the whole situation, only part of it.\n\nFor your writeup, you can literally use:\n\u201cEvaluation: We report pass^k over at least 3 seeds. pass^k equals 1 only if the agent succeeds on all k runs, so it measures reliability.\u201d\n\u201cThis environment is a POMDP because the assistant only observes part of the full state and must take actions to reveal more information.\u201d\n\nIf you want, just reply with what part still feels confusing: pass^k or POMDP.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-environment"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pomdp?\n[activity] t=32 messages 1m", "t": 33, "activity": [{"t": 32, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.5436465175835687, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.75, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7764817897604411, "motivation": 0.264715486329607, "reliance": 0.6964404438934201, "persistence": 0.31214034943975877, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 2.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.2391749169999997, "seen_posts": ["p6", "p3"], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791258937.3507369, "type": "step", "step": 37, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 the answer is: a POMDP is a Partially Observable Markov Decision Process, meaning the agent cannot directly see the full true state and only gets partial observations. In your build, the assistant does not automatically know the whole computer/student state; it only sees what is on screen or what it opens, so it must act under uncertainty and gather information. A one-sentence writeup version is: \u201cThis environment is a POMDP because the assistant only observes part of the underlying state and must take actions to reveal more.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-environment"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=33 messages 1m", "t": 34, "activity": [{"t": 33, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.547668982914794, "pass_k": 0.45874216847287114}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.75, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7764817897604411, "motivation": 0.21471548632960702, "reliance": 0.77644044389342, "persistence": 0.28214034943975874, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 2.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.2674224418999995, "seen_posts": ["p6", "p3"], "extra": {}}}
